---
id: PY-002
type: rule
family: python-reliability
title: 'bare # noqa without a rule code'
version: 1

severity: warning
confidence: high
spectrum_position: 4

targets: [source]
file_extensions: [.py]
allowlist: ['**/test_*.py', '**/*_test.py', '**/tests/**', '**/conftest.py', '**/explain/**']

detection:
  type: regex
  pattern: '#\s*noqa([^:]|$)'

related: [PY-001]
enabled: true
opt_in: false
---

A bare `# noqa` disables every lint rule on this line, so a real defect added
here later will never be reported. Name the rule you mean to silence:
`# noqa: E501`. If several apply, list them: `# noqa: E501,F401`.
